-- title:
--   Cyclotomic Birman–Wenzl algebra $\mathscr B_{r,n}$, u-admissible parameters, $N_r$, $Q_{r,\varrho}$, $S_{r,\varrho}$ and the Ariki–Koike algebra $\mathscr H_{r,n}$ (pp. 2–5, 24)
-- statement:
--   This file fixes the objects of Rui and Si's semisimplicity criterion, over an arbitrary field $F$.
--
--   **Parameters (Assumption 2.2, p. 2).** Fix integers $r, n$, an element $q \in F$, a family $u = (u_1,\dots,u_r)$ of elements of $F$ and a sign $\varepsilon \in \{1,-1\}$. Put $\delta = q - q^{-1}$ and
--   $$\alpha = \begin{cases} \varepsilon, & r \text{ odd},\\ \varepsilon q^{-\varepsilon}, & r \text{ even},\end{cases}\qquad \varrho^{-1} = \alpha \prod_{\ell=1}^r u_\ell,$$
--   so that $\alpha \in \{1,-1\}$ for odd $r$ and $\alpha \in \{q^{-1}, -q\}$ for even $r$, as in Assumption 2.2(2). With $\gamma_r(x) = 1$ for odd $r$ and $\gamma_r(x) = -x$ for even $r$, set
--   $$\gamma_i = \Big(\gamma_r(u_i) + \delta^{-1}\varrho\,(u_i^2-1)\prod_{j\ne i}u_j\Big)\prod_{j \ne i}\frac{u_iu_j-1}{u_i-u_j},\qquad \omega_a = \sum_{j=1}^r u_j^a\gamma_j \quad (a \in \mathbb Z).$$
--   These are exactly the u-admissible parameters of Assumption 2.2; for them $\omega_0 = 1 - \delta^{-1}(\varrho - \varrho^{-1})$, the value used in the first paragraph of §2.
--
--   **The algebra (Definition 2.1, p. 2).** $\mathscr B_{r,n}$ is the unital associative $F$-algebra generated by $T_i, E_i$ ($1 \le i < n$) and $X_j^{\pm 1}$ ($1 \le j \le n$) subject to: a) $X_iX_i^{-1} = X_i^{-1}X_i = 1$; b) $1 = T_i^2 - \delta T_i + \delta\varrho E_i$; c) $T_iT_j = T_jT_i$ for $|i-j|>1$, $T_iT_{i+1}T_i = T_{i+1}T_iT_{i+1}$, $T_iX_j = X_jT_i$ for $j \ne i, i+1$; d) $E_i^2 = \omega_0E_i$; e) $X_iX_j = X_jX_i$; f) $T_iX_i - X_{i+1}T_i = \delta X_{i+1}(E_i-1)$ and $X_iT_i - T_iX_{i+1} = \delta(E_i-1)X_{i+1}$; g) $E_1X_1^aE_1 = \omega_aE_1$ for all $a \in \mathbb Z$; h) $E_iT_i = \varrho E_i = T_iE_i$ and $E_{i+1}E_i = E_{i+1}T_iT_{i+1} = T_iT_{i+1}E_i$; i) $E_{i+1}E_iE_{i+1} = E_{i+1}$, $E_iE_{i+1}E_i = E_i$; j) $E_iX_iX_{i+1} = E_i = X_iX_{i+1}E_i$; k) $(X_1-u_1)\cdots(X_1-u_r) = 0$, with the index ranges of the paper.
--
--   **Derived objects.** $\mathscr B_{r,m} \subseteq \mathscr B_{r,n}$ ($m \le n$) is the subalgebra generated by $T_i, E_i$ ($i < m$) and $X_j^{\pm1}$ ($j \le m$), the image of the natural map of p. 5 (for $m = 0$ it is $F\cdot 1$); $E_{f,n} = E_{n-1}E_{n-3}\cdots E_{n-2f+1}$ (p. 4). $N_r$ is the set (2.3) of $r$ consecutive integers $-\lfloor r/2\rfloor + \tfrac12(1+(-1)^r) \le i \le \lfloor r/2 \rfloor$, and $\mathcal H = (\omega_{a+b})_{a,b \in N_r}$ is the associated Hankel matrix. The sets of (6.6)–(6.7), p. 24, are
--   $$Q_{r,\varrho} = \begin{cases}\{-\varepsilon q, \varepsilon q^{-1}\}, & r \text{ odd},\\ \{-q^{\varepsilon}, q^{\varepsilon}\}, & r \text{ even},\end{cases}\qquad S_{r,\varrho} = \begin{cases}\bigcup_{k=3}^n\{\pm q^{3-k}, \pm q^{k-3}, \varepsilon q^{3-2k}, -\varepsilon q^{2k-3}\}, & r\text{ odd},\\ \bigcup_{k=3}^n\{\pm q^{3-k}, \pm q^{k-3}, \pm q^{(2k-3)\varepsilon}\}, & r \text{ even},\end{cases}$$
--   together with $D_n = \bigcup_{k=3}^n\{q^{4-2k}, q^{2k-4}\}$ of Theorem 6.8(b)(2)(d). The condition $o(q^2) > n$ means $q^{2k} \ne 1$ for $1 \le k \le n$, and **Ariki's condition** at level $n$ means $|d| \ge n$ whenever $u_iu_j^{-1} = q^{2d}$ with $1 \le i < j \le r$ and $d \in \mathbb Z$.
--
--   **The Ariki–Koike algebra (p. 3).** $\mathscr H_{r,n}$ is the unital $F$-algebra generated by $g_1,\dots,g_{n-1}$, $y_1,\dots,y_n$ subject to $(g_i-q)(g_i+q^{-1}) = 0$, the braid relations, $g_iy_j = y_jg_i$ for $j \ne i,i+1$, $y_iy_j = y_jy_i$, $y_{i+1} = g_iy_ig_i$ and $(y_1-u_1)\cdots(y_1-u_r) = 0$.
--
--   These objects are the common ground of every statement of the mission.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The algebras are `RingQuot` quotients of free algebras. Indices are 0-based: the Lean generator `T i` is the paper's $T_{i+1}$, and similarly for $E$, $X$, $g$, $y$. The inverse $X_j^{-1}$ is a separate generator `Xinv j` tied to `X j` by relation a); $X_1^a$ for $a<0$ is a power of `Xinv 0`. The sign $\varepsilon$ is an element of $\mathbb Z^\times$, and $\alpha, \varrho, \gamma_i, \omega_a$ are computed from $(q,u,\varepsilon)$, so the parameters are u-admissible by construction. Relations d) and g) both use $\omega_0 = \sum_j\gamma_j$, which equals $1 - \delta^{-1}(\varrho - \varrho^{-1})$ for these parameters. $\gamma_i$ divides by $u_i - u_j$, so the theorems assume the $u_i$ pairwise distinct. The index $a \in N_r$ of the Hankel matrix is the Lean index $a - \min N_r \in \{0,\dots,r-1\}$.
-- source:
--   Rui and Si, The representation theory of cyclotomic BMW algebras, arXiv:0807.4149v1, p. 2, Definition 2.1, Assumption 2.2; p. 3, Ariki–Koike algebra, (2.3); pp. 4–5, E_{f,n} and B_{r,m} ⊆ B_{r,n}; p. 24, (6.6)–(6.7); pp. 24–25, Theorem 6.8 conditions

import Mathlib

/-!
Rui and Si, *The representation theory of cyclotomic BMW algebras*, arXiv:0807.4149v1.
Parameters and u-admissibility (Assumption 2.2, p. 2), the cyclotomic Birman–Wenzl algebra
`B_{r,n}` (Definition 2.1, p. 2), the Ariki–Koike algebra `H_{r,n}` (p. 3), the index set `N_r`
((2.3), p. 3), the subalgebras `B_{r,m} ⊆ B_{r,n}` (p. 5), `E_{f,n}` (p. 4), and the sets
`Q_{r,ϱ}`, `S_{r,ϱ}` ((6.6)–(6.7), p. 24), all over a field `F`.

Conventions. The paper's indices are 1-based, Lean's are 0-based: the Lean generator with
index `i` is the paper's generator with index `i + 1`. The inverse `X_j⁻¹` is a separate
generator `Xinv j`, tied to `X j` by relation a). The sign `ε ∈ {1, -1}` is the free parameter;
`α`, `ϱ`, `γ_i` and `ω_a` are computed from `(q, u, ε)` exactly as in Assumption 2.2, so the
parameters are u-admissible by construction. `γ_i` divides by `u_i - u_j`; the theorems assume
the `u_i` pairwise distinct. Relations d) and g) both use `ω_0 = ∑_j γ_j`, which equals the
paper's `1 - δ⁻¹(ϱ - ϱ⁻¹)` for these parameters.
-/

namespace CycBMW.Semisimple

noncomputable section

open scoped BigOperators

section Parameters

variable {F : Type*} [Field F]

/-- `δ = q - q⁻¹` (p. 2). -/
def delta (q : F) : F := q - q⁻¹

/-- `α` of Assumption 2.2(2), indexed by the sign `ε`: `α = ε` if `r` is odd, and
`α = ε q^{-ε}` if `r` is even (that is `q⁻¹` for `ε = 1` and `-q` for `ε = -1`). -/
def alpha (r : ℕ) (q : F) (ε : ℤˣ) : F :=
  if Even r then ((ε : ℤ) : F) * q ^ (-(ε : ℤ)) else ((ε : ℤ) : F)

/-- `ϱ` with `ϱ⁻¹ = α ∏_ℓ u_ℓ` (Assumption 2.2). -/
def rho (r : ℕ) (q : F) (u : Fin r → F) (ε : ℤˣ) : F :=
  (alpha r q ε * ∏ l, u l)⁻¹

/-- `γ_r(x) = 1` if `r` is odd and `-x` if `r` is even (p. 2). -/
def gammaR (r : ℕ) (x : F) : F := if Even r then -x else 1

/-- `γ_i` of Assumption 2.2(1). -/
def gamma (r : ℕ) (q : F) (u : Fin r → F) (ε : ℤˣ) (i : Fin r) : F :=
  (gammaR r (u i) + (delta q)⁻¹ * rho r q u ε * (u i ^ 2 - 1) *
      ∏ j ∈ Finset.univ.erase i, u j) *
    ∏ j ∈ Finset.univ.erase i, (u i * u j - 1) / (u i - u j)

/-- `ω_a = ∑_j u_j^a γ_j` for `a ∈ ℤ` (Assumption 2.2). -/
def omega (r : ℕ) (q : F) (u : Fin r → F) (ε : ℤˣ) (a : ℤ) : F :=
  ∑ j, u j ^ a * gamma r q u ε j

/-- The least element of `N_r = {i ∈ ℤ : -⌊r/2⌋ + (1 + (-1)^r)/2 ≤ i ≤ ⌊r/2⌋}` ((2.3), p. 3);
`N_r` consists of the `r` consecutive integers starting here. -/
def nMin (r : ℕ) : ℤ := if Even r then 1 - ((r / 2 : ℕ) : ℤ) else -((r / 2 : ℕ) : ℤ)

/-- The Hankel matrix `(ω_{a+b})_{a,b ∈ N_r}`, indexed by `Fin r` via `a ↦ nMin r + a`. -/
def hankel (r : ℕ) (q : F) (u : Fin r → F) (ε : ℤˣ) : Matrix (Fin r) (Fin r) F :=
  fun a b => omega r q u ε (2 * nMin r + (a : ℤ) + (b : ℤ))

/-- `Q_{r,ϱ}` of (6.6): `{-εq, εq⁻¹}` if `r` is odd, `{-q^ε, q^ε}` if `r` is even. -/
def Qset (r : ℕ) (q : F) (ε : ℤˣ) : Set F :=
  if Even r then {-(q ^ (ε : ℤ)), q ^ (ε : ℤ)}
  else {-(((ε : ℤ) : F) * q), ((ε : ℤ) : F) * q⁻¹}

/-- `S_{r,ϱ}` of (6.7): the union over `3 ≤ k ≤ n` of
`{±q^{3-k}, ±q^{k-3}, εq^{3-2k}, -εq^{2k-3}}` if `r` is odd and of
`{±q^{3-k}, ±q^{k-3}, ±q^{(2k-3)ε}}` if `r` is even. -/
def Sset (r n : ℕ) (q : F) (ε : ℤˣ) : Set F :=
  ⋃ k : ℕ, ⋃ (_ : 3 ≤ k ∧ k ≤ n),
    if Even r then
      {q ^ (3 - (k : ℤ)), -(q ^ (3 - (k : ℤ))), q ^ ((k : ℤ) - 3), -(q ^ ((k : ℤ) - 3)),
        q ^ ((2 * (k : ℤ) - 3) * (ε : ℤ)), -(q ^ ((2 * (k : ℤ) - 3) * (ε : ℤ)))}
    else
      {q ^ (3 - (k : ℤ)), -(q ^ (3 - (k : ℤ))), q ^ ((k : ℤ) - 3), -(q ^ ((k : ℤ) - 3)),
        ((ε : ℤ) : F) * q ^ (3 - 2 * (k : ℤ)), -(((ε : ℤ) : F) * q ^ (2 * (k : ℤ) - 3))}

/-- `⋃_{k=3}^n {q^{4-2k}, q^{2k-4}}`, condition (d) of Theorem 6.8(b)(2). -/
def Dset (n : ℕ) (q : F) : Set F :=
  ⋃ k : ℕ, ⋃ (_ : 3 ≤ k ∧ k ≤ n), {q ^ (4 - 2 * (k : ℤ)), q ^ (2 * (k : ℤ) - 4)}

/-- `o(q²) > n`, written as `q^{2k} ≠ 1` for `1 ≤ k ≤ n` (no `orderOf`). -/
def OrderGt (q : F) (n : ℕ) : Prop := ∀ k : ℕ, 1 ≤ k → k ≤ n → q ^ (2 * k) ≠ 1

/-- Ariki's condition: `|d| ≥ n` whenever `u_i u_j⁻¹ = q^{2d}`, `1 ≤ i < j ≤ r`, `d ∈ ℤ`. -/
def ArikiCond {r : ℕ} (q : F) (u : Fin r → F) (n : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∀ i j : Fin r, i < j → ∀ d : ℤ, u i * (u j)⁻¹ = q ^ (2 * d) → (n : ℤ) ≤ |d|

end Parameters

/-! ### The cyclotomic Birman–Wenzl algebra `B_{r,n}` (Definition 2.1) -/

/-- Generators: `T i`, `E i` (`i : Fin (n - 1)`, the paper's `T_{i+1}`, `E_{i+1}`), `X j` and
`Xinv j` (`j : Fin n`, the paper's `X_{j+1}` and `X_{j+1}⁻¹`). -/
inductive Gen (n : ℕ) where
  | T : Fin (n - 1) → Gen n
  | E : Fin (n - 1) → Gen n
  | X : Fin n → Gen n
  | Xinv : Fin n → Gen n

section Free

variable (F : Type*) [Field F] (n : ℕ)

/-- Free `T_{i+1}`; only `i < n - 1` is used. -/
def fT (i : ℕ) : FreeAlgebra F (Gen n) :=
  if h : i < n - 1 then FreeAlgebra.ι F (Gen.T ⟨i, h⟩) else 0

/-- Free `E_{i+1}`; only `i < n - 1` is used. -/
def fE (i : ℕ) : FreeAlgebra F (Gen n) :=
  if h : i < n - 1 then FreeAlgebra.ι F (Gen.E ⟨i, h⟩) else 0

/-- Free `X_{j+1}`; only `j < n` is used. -/
def fX (j : ℕ) : FreeAlgebra F (Gen n) :=
  if h : j < n then FreeAlgebra.ι F (Gen.X ⟨j, h⟩) else 0

/-- Free `X_{j+1}⁻¹`; only `j < n` is used. -/
def fXinv (j : ℕ) : FreeAlgebra F (Gen n) :=
  if h : j < n then FreeAlgebra.ι F (Gen.Xinv ⟨j, h⟩) else 0

/-- Free `X_{j+1}^a` for `a ∈ ℤ`, using `Xinv` for negative `a`. -/
def fXpow (j : ℕ) (a : ℤ) : FreeAlgebra F (Gen n) :=
  if 0 ≤ a then fX F n j ^ a.toNat else fXinv F n j ^ (-a).toNat

end Free

section Relations

variable {F : Type*} [Field F]

/-- The relations a)–k) of Definition 2.1, with 0-based indices. -/
inductive Rel (r n : ℕ) (q : F) (u : Fin r → F) (ε : ℤˣ) :
    FreeAlgebra F (Gen n) → FreeAlgebra F (Gen n) → Prop
  /- a) `X_i X_i⁻¹ = X_i⁻¹ X_i = 1`. -/
  | a_left (i : ℕ) (hi : i < n) : Rel r n q u ε (fX F n i * fXinv F n i) 1
  | a_right (i : ℕ) (hi : i < n) : Rel r n q u ε (fXinv F n i * fX F n i) 1
  /- b) `1 = T_i² - δ T_i + δ ϱ E_i`. -/
  | b (i : ℕ) (hi : i < n - 1) :
      Rel r n q u ε
        (fT F n i ^ 2 - algebraMap F _ (delta q) * fT F n i +
          algebraMap F _ (delta q * rho r q u ε) * fE F n i) 1
  /- c)(i) `T_i T_j = T_j T_i` if `|i - j| > 1`. -/
  | c_i (i j : ℕ) (hi : i < n - 1) (hj : j < n - 1) (hij : i + 1 < j ∨ j + 1 < i) :
      Rel r n q u ε (fT F n i * fT F n j) (fT F n j * fT F n i)
  /- c)(ii) `T_i T_{i+1} T_i = T_{i+1} T_i T_{i+1}`. -/
  | c_ii (i : ℕ) (hi : i + 1 < n - 1) :
      Rel r n q u ε (fT F n i * fT F n (i + 1) * fT F n i)
        (fT F n (i + 1) * fT F n i * fT F n (i + 1))
  /- c)(iii) `T_i X_j = X_j T_i` if `j ≠ i, i + 1`. -/
  | c_iii (i j : ℕ) (hi : i < n - 1) (hj : j < n) (hji : j ≠ i) (hji' : j ≠ i + 1) :
      Rel r n q u ε (fT F n i * fX F n j) (fX F n j * fT F n i)
  /- d) `E_i² = ω_0 E_i`. -/
  | d (i : ℕ) (hi : i < n - 1) :
      Rel r n q u ε (fE F n i ^ 2) (algebraMap F _ (omega r q u ε 0) * fE F n i)
  /- e) `X_i X_j = X_j X_i`. -/
  | e (i j : ℕ) (hi : i < n) (hj : j < n) :
      Rel r n q u ε (fX F n i * fX F n j) (fX F n j * fX F n i)
  /- f)(i) `T_i X_i - X_{i+1} T_i = δ X_{i+1} (E_i - 1)`. -/
  | f_i (i : ℕ) (hi : i < n - 1) :
      Rel r n q u ε (fT F n i * fX F n i - fX F n (i + 1) * fT F n i)
        (algebraMap F _ (delta q) * fX F n (i + 1) * (fE F n i - 1))
  /- f)(ii) `X_i T_i - T_i X_{i+1} = δ (E_i - 1) X_{i+1}`. -/
  | f_ii (i : ℕ) (hi : i < n - 1) :
      Rel r n q u ε (fX F n i * fT F n i - fT F n i * fX F n (i + 1))
        (algebraMap F _ (delta q) * (fE F n i - 1) * fX F n (i + 1))
  /- g) `E_1 X_1^a E_1 = ω_a E_1` for `a ∈ ℤ` (only when `E_1` exists, `n ≥ 2`). -/
  | g (a : ℤ) (hn : 2 ≤ n) :
      Rel r n q u ε (fE F n 0 * fXpow F n 0 a * fE F n 0)
        (algebraMap F _ (omega r q u ε a) * fE F n 0)
  /- h)(i) `E_i T_i = ϱ E_i = T_i E_i`. -/
  | h_i_left (i : ℕ) (hi : i < n - 1) :
      Rel r n q u ε (fE F n i * fT F n i) (algebraMap F _ (rho r q u ε) * fE F n i)
  | h_i_right (i : ℕ) (hi : i < n - 1) :
      Rel r n q u ε (fT F n i * fE F n i) (algebraMap F _ (rho r q u ε) * fE F n i)
  /- h)(ii) `E_{i+1} E_i = E_{i+1} T_i T_{i+1} = T_i T_{i+1} E_i`. -/
  | h_ii_left (i : ℕ) (hi : i + 1 < n - 1) :
      Rel r n q u ε (fE F n (i + 1) * fE F n i) (fE F n (i + 1) * fT F n i * fT F n (i + 1))
  | h_ii_right (i : ℕ) (hi : i + 1 < n - 1) :
      Rel r n q u ε (fE F n (i + 1) * fE F n i) (fT F n i * fT F n (i + 1) * fE F n i)
  /- i)(i) `E_{i+1} E_i E_{i+1} = E_{i+1}`. -/
  | i_i (i : ℕ) (hi : i + 1 < n - 1) :
      Rel r n q u ε (fE F n (i + 1) * fE F n i * fE F n (i + 1)) (fE F n (i + 1))
  /- i)(ii) `E_i E_{i+1} E_i = E_i`. -/
  | i_ii (i : ℕ) (hi : i + 1 < n - 1) :
      Rel r n q u ε (fE F n i * fE F n (i + 1) * fE F n i) (fE F n i)
  /- j) `E_i X_i X_{i+1} = E_i = X_i X_{i+1} E_i`. -/
  | j_left (i : ℕ) (hi : i < n - 1) :
      Rel r n q u ε (fE F n i * fX F n i * fX F n (i + 1)) (fE F n i)
  | j_right (i : ℕ) (hi : i < n - 1) :
      Rel r n q u ε (fX F n i * fX F n (i + 1) * fE F n i) (fE F n i)
  /- k) `(X_1 - u_1) ⋯ (X_1 - u_r) = 0`. -/
  | k (hn : 1 ≤ n) :
      Rel r n q u ε ((List.ofFn fun l : Fin r => fX F n 0 - algebraMap F _ (u l)).prod) 0

end Relations

/-- The cyclotomic Birman–Wenzl algebra `B_{r,n}` over the field `F` (Definition 2.1). -/
abbrev B (F : Type*) [Field F] (r n : ℕ) (q : F) (u : Fin r → F) (ε : ℤˣ) : Type _ :=
  RingQuot (Rel (F := F) r n q u ε)

section Generators

variable (F : Type*) [Field F] (r n : ℕ) (q : F) (u : Fin r → F) (ε : ℤˣ)

/-- `T_{i+1} ∈ B_{r,n}`. -/
def T (i : Fin (n - 1)) : B F r n q u ε :=
  RingQuot.mkAlgHom F (Rel (F := F) r n q u ε) (FreeAlgebra.ι F (Gen.T i))

/-- `E_{i+1} ∈ B_{r,n}`. -/
def E (i : Fin (n - 1)) : B F r n q u ε :=
  RingQuot.mkAlgHom F (Rel (F := F) r n q u ε) (FreeAlgebra.ι F (Gen.E i))

/-- `X_{j+1} ∈ B_{r,n}`. -/
def X (j : Fin n) : B F r n q u ε :=
  RingQuot.mkAlgHom F (Rel (F := F) r n q u ε) (FreeAlgebra.ι F (Gen.X j))

/-- `X_{j+1}⁻¹ ∈ B_{r,n}`. -/
def Xinv (j : Fin n) : B F r n q u ε :=
  RingQuot.mkAlgHom F (Rel (F := F) r n q u ε) (FreeAlgebra.ι F (Gen.Xinv j))

/-- `E_{i+1}` addressed by a natural-number index (`0` when `i ≥ n - 1`, never used so). -/
def Eat (i : ℕ) : B F r n q u ε :=
  if h : i < n - 1 then E F r n q u ε ⟨i, h⟩ else 0

/-- `B_{r,m} ⊆ B_{r,n}` (p. 5): the subalgebra generated by `T_i, E_i` (`1 ≤ i < m`) and
`X_j^{±1}` (`1 ≤ j ≤ m`), i.e. the image of the natural map `B_{r,m} → B_{r,n}`.
For `m = 0` it is `F · 1`. -/
def Bsub (m : ℕ) : Subalgebra F (B F r n q u ε) :=
  Algebra.adjoin F
    ({x | ∃ i : Fin (n - 1), i.val + 1 < m ∧ (x = T F r n q u ε i ∨ x = E F r n q u ε i)} ∪
      {x | ∃ j : Fin n, j.val < m ∧ (x = X F r n q u ε j ∨ x = Xinv F r n q u ε j)})

/-- `E_{f,n} = E_{n-1} E_{n-3} ⋯ E_{n-2f+1}` (paper indices; p. 4). In 0-based indices the
factors are `E (n-2), E (n-4), …, E (n-2f)`, in this order. -/
def Efn (f : ℕ) : B F r n q u ε :=
  (List.ofFn fun k : Fin f => Eat F r n q u ε (n - 2 - 2 * k.val)).prod

end Generators

/-! ### The Ariki–Koike algebra `H_{r,n}` (p. 3) -/

/-- Generators `g i` (`i : Fin (n - 1)`, the paper's `g_{i+1}`) and `y j` (`j : Fin n`, the
paper's `y_{j+1}`). -/
inductive AKGen (n : ℕ) where
  | g : Fin (n - 1) → AKGen n
  | y : Fin n → AKGen n

section AK

variable (F : Type*) [Field F] (n : ℕ)

/-- Free `g_{i+1}`; only `i < n - 1` is used. -/
def fg (i : ℕ) : FreeAlgebra F (AKGen n) :=
  if h : i < n - 1 then FreeAlgebra.ι F (AKGen.g ⟨i, h⟩) else 0

/-- Free `y_{j+1}`; only `j < n` is used. -/
def fy (j : ℕ) : FreeAlgebra F (AKGen n) :=
  if h : j < n then FreeAlgebra.ι F (AKGen.y ⟨j, h⟩) else 0

end AK

/-- The relations a)–g) of the Ariki–Koike algebra (p. 3), with 0-based indices. -/
inductive AKRel {F : Type*} [Field F] (r n : ℕ) (q : F) (u : Fin r → F) :
    FreeAlgebra F (AKGen n) → FreeAlgebra F (AKGen n) → Prop
  /- a) `(g_i - q)(g_i + q⁻¹) = 0`. -/
  | a (i : ℕ) (hi : i < n - 1) :
      AKRel r n q u ((fg F n i - algebraMap F _ q) * (fg F n i + algebraMap F _ q⁻¹)) 0
  /- b) `g_i g_j = g_j g_i` if `|i - j| > 1`. -/
  | b (i j : ℕ) (hi : i < n - 1) (hj : j < n - 1) (hij : i + 1 < j ∨ j + 1 < i) :
      AKRel r n q u (fg F n i * fg F n j) (fg F n j * fg F n i)
  /- c) `g_i g_{i+1} g_i = g_{i+1} g_i g_{i+1}`. -/
  | c (i : ℕ) (hi : i + 1 < n - 1) :
      AKRel r n q u (fg F n i * fg F n (i + 1) * fg F n i)
        (fg F n (i + 1) * fg F n i * fg F n (i + 1))
  /- d) `g_i y_j = y_j g_i` if `j ≠ i, i + 1`. -/
  | d (i j : ℕ) (hi : i < n - 1) (hj : j < n) (hji : j ≠ i) (hji' : j ≠ i + 1) :
      AKRel r n q u (fg F n i * fy F n j) (fy F n j * fg F n i)
  /- e) `y_i y_j = y_j y_i`. -/
  | e (i j : ℕ) (hi : i < n) (hj : j < n) :
      AKRel r n q u (fy F n i * fy F n j) (fy F n j * fy F n i)
  /- f) `y_{i+1} = g_i y_i g_i`. -/
  | f (i : ℕ) (hi : i < n - 1) :
      AKRel r n q u (fy F n (i + 1)) (fg F n i * fy F n i * fg F n i)
  /- g) `(y_1 - u_1) ⋯ (y_1 - u_r) = 0`. -/
  | g (hn : 1 ≤ n) :
      AKRel r n q u ((List.ofFn fun l : Fin r => fy F n 0 - algebraMap F _ (u l)).prod) 0

/-- The Ariki–Koike algebra `H_{r,n}` over `F` (p. 3). -/
abbrev H (F : Type*) [Field F] (r n : ℕ) (q : F) (u : Fin r → F) : Type _ :=
  RingQuot (AKRel (F := F) r n q u)

end

end CycBMW.Semisimple


